      "id": "function:yosoi::request::Attempt::body_bytes",
      "publicPath": "yosoi::request::Attempt::body_bytes",
      "title": "yosoi::request::Attempt::body_bytes",
      "kind": "function",
      "signature": "pub fn body_bytes(self) -> Option<&'response [u8]>",
      "docs": "Borrows the complete retained Direct HTTP body after content decoding.\n\nBytes are independent of document projection and character decoding, so\nICO, PNG and other binary media do not require a searchable Document.\nThe response-document selection must have retained the source. Returns\n`None` for incomplete or unavailable bodies, failed/unstarted attempts,\nbrowser acquisitions, or an omitted response-document selection. A retained\nempty body is `Some(&[])`. Inspect status separately: an HTTP error response\ncan still have a complete body. Source byte limits continue to apply.",
      "source": {
        "file": "crates/yosoi/src/request/outcomes.rs",
